# Every text file in this repository is stored with LF endings, and the working
# tree keeps LF too (the project is cross-platform and Windows tools here — git,
# cargo, rustfmt, PowerShell — all accept LF). Declaring it explicitly means an
# editor or script that rewrites a file with CRLF cannot silently turn a one-line
# change into a whole-file diff.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Git's text detection is heuristic; these are binary regardless of content.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.exe binary
*.redb binary
*.lock binary
